# Yalb Maeger

Maeger is the minimal Windows build of Yalb Browser, built with C# WinForms and Microsoft Edge WebView2.

Start page: https://origin.mozartt.workers.dev/
Repository: https://github.com/Initial-Mozartt/Yalb

## Features

- WebView2 browsing with multiple tabs.
- Top tab bar by default, with optional sidebar tab mode.
- Icon-only tool sidebar for bookmarks, history, downloads, and settings.
- Floating address bar with keyboard-first navigation.
- Session restore, local history, and JSON settings.
- Frameless and fullscreen controls.

## Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|----------|--------|
| `Ctrl+T` | New tab |
| `Ctrl+W` | Close current tab |
| `Ctrl+L` | Toggle floating address bar |
| `Ctrl+R` / `F5` | Reload |
| `Ctrl+H` | Home |
| `Ctrl+Left` / `Ctrl+[` | Back |
| `Ctrl+Right` / `Ctrl+]` | Forward |
| `Ctrl+Tab` | Next tab |
| `Ctrl+Shift+Tab` | Previous tab |
| `F11` | Toggle full screen |
| `Ctrl+Alt+F` | Toggle frameless window |
| `Ctrl+Shift+B` | Toggle browser chrome |
| `Ctrl+Shift+Alt+F` | Full frameless |

## Project Layout

```text
Maeger/
├── Yalb.Maeger.csproj
├── Program.cs
├── BrowserForm.cs
├── OriginSettings.cs
├── YalbSettings.cs
├── chrome-ui/
├── pages/
└── Splash/
```

## Build

```bash
cd Maeger
dotnet build Yalb.Maeger.csproj
dotnet run --project Yalb.Maeger.csproj
```

## Publish

```bash
dotnet publish Yalb.Maeger.csproj -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained true -p:PublishSingleFile=true -o ./publish
```

