## Building the Startpage

Prerequisites:

- Node.js 20.x (use `nvm` to manage versions)
- `pnpm` (install via `npm install -g pnpm`)
- PowerShell 7+ (for the native installer script)

Quick setup (Windows):

```powershell
# switch to Node 20
nvm install 20.20.2
nvm use 20.20.2

# ensure TEMP is on a drive with space (optional)
$env:TEMP = 'D:\Temp'
$env:TMP  = 'D:\Temp'

# set npm cache to a drive with space
npm config set cache D:\npm-cache --global

cd ..\startpage-src
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force node_modules -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
Remove-Item -Force pnpm-lock.yaml -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
pnpm install
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\install-windows-native.ps1
pnpm --filter @workspace/startpage run build
```

The build artifacts will be in `startpage-src\artifacts\startpage\dist` and the MSBuild target in the project copies them into the application output under `startpage/dist` during `dotnet build`.
